d-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/122598-mortal-remains-is-here?p=123774#post123774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A gentleman, a scholar and a saint of PDFs as always you are, Mr Gone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! If all goes well I'll work on it tomorrow. I'm still working on a new Demon sheet, but I think I can knock this out alittle quicker. If I get it done tomorrow I'll post it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T08:22:54-07:00","id":123795,"title":"","content":"After reading the Demon chapter I'm very tempted to make the Malleus Maleficarum into a God-Machine Cult and have Benedictions be a weird form of Stigmata. Could work with the idea that a lot of the Christian &quot;infrastructure&quot; scattered around the world is what makes them work.<br /> <br /> Also, am I the only one thinking that the Knights of St Adrian might not be Stigmatics, but just people carrying around aspects of the Angel that sorts out their ink ala the way Demons can give human gadgets and have them work? <br /> <br /> Also the Lucifuge entry seemed a little...all over the place I guess. Hopefully Heirs to Hell will expand on the relationship between the Unchained, their kids and the Lucifuge a bit more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T09:18:44-07:00","id":123813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/122598-mortal-remains-is-here?p=123758#post123758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still have no idea who you're talking about. I like to think I'm fairly well versed in the lore, but this stray fact just doesn't exist anywhere. In which book is it?(In this way, I might still be right)</div> </div> </div> </div>Read the second part of the post again <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Ivanovich is probaly going to be in my next piece of Hunter homebrew. I might rename him though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T09:58:23-07:00","id":123829,"title":"","content":"Ok, could someone please explain to me just who the Knights of St. Adrian are? Because all I've got so far is that they're ridiculous 80s action heroes. Which sounds a little too... ridiculous for this level of love. Don't get me wrong, I love ridiculous, but it tends not to mesh all that well with standard WoD fluff. So what's so great about them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2449-one-tin-soldier","name":"One Tin Soldier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2449_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T09:58:42-07:00","id":123830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/122598-mortal-remains-is-here?p=123813#post123813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Read the second part of the post again <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Ivanovich is probaly going to be in my next piece of Hunter homebrew. I might rename him though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. In that case, yes, it's <i>exactly</i> what I thought it was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T10:01:22-07:00","id":123832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Tin Soldier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/122598-mortal-remains-is-here?p=123829#post123829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, could someone please explain to me just who the Knights of St. Adrian are? Because all I've got so far is that they're ridiculous 80s action heroes. Which sounds a little too... ridiculous for this level of love. Don't get me wrong, I love ridiculous, but it tends not to mesh all that well with standard WoD fluff. So what's so great about them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know where you get that idea, they're more like Dog the Bounty Hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T10:13:08-07:00","id":123842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/122598-mortal-remains-is-here?p=123830#post123830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah. In that case, yes, it's <i>exactly</i> what I thought it was.</div> </div> </div> </div>Feel the dread. Mwahahahaha. (Actually, why dread?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T12:33:29-07:00","id":123935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Tin Soldier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/122598-mortal-remains-is-here?p=123829#post123829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, could someone please explain to me just who the Knights of St. Adrian are? Because all I've got so far is that they're ridiculous 80s action heroes. Which sounds a little too... ridiculous for this level of love. Don't get me wrong, I love ridiculous, but it tends not to mesh all that well with standard WoD fluff. So what's so great about them?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Knights of Saint Adrian, or the Sidearm of the Angels, are essentially bounty hunters for 'Heaven'(It might be a God Machine plot, or it might actually be some other divinity wearing the same face) who hunt down demons with the power of their angelic tattoos.<br /> <br /> There's a few reasons for the love. First off is that it is a very bold and upfront conspiracy, even if the 80s action hero <i>is</i> somewhat taking it too far. They don't have a complex motivation for what they do-they're demons and it's a paycheck and it's much like hunting down any other criminal as a bounty hunter, a certain bluntness is needed. The way they approach their jobs as hunter, as dictated by the Ink Endowment, is similarly blunt-three of the eight directly tie into brawl and require, you know, actually hitting someone(although the third one, LOVE/HATE, has a twofer purpose, and only one is violent), with a fourth one that basically makes you as superior in some trait(Namely-Strength, Dexterity, Brawl, Weaponry, Firearms) as the last guy you fought. They can have a certain amount of infinite resources in regards to firearms and vehicles, which invites reckless use thereof-you can totally smash a car into a building and not worry about it. The remaining ones might be....subtler? But it's just a refreshingly straightforward group with a no-nonsense attitude that, mixed in with a bit of vicious cunning, is very effective.<br /> <br /> That bluntness might not be so appealing...if it wasn't for the fact that <i>their enemies are demons</i> and that it <i>actually works</i>. Something this unsubtle shouldn't even be able to touch the Unchained(or your world's equivalent), but all it takes it one hit to start some serious momentum<br /> <br /> I'm not saying they can't be smart, or cunning-on the contrary, I think a lot of them actually are. They are, after all, bounty hunters, probably for normal criminals in between the demons as well. But when they take the stage, when they act, it's with the zeal of angels without the stigma of religious culture-rather, their zeal might seem angelic for its' potency, but it's born from road culture, bar fights, and a general salt of the earth background.<br /> <br /> They're also refreshingly honest on the whole. Sure, something's screwing with them and pulling strings, but go below the client and there' actually very little the group faffs around with. It's a stark contrast from nearly every other Conspiracy there is.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. I think that's why.EDIT: or even simpler, it walks the line between heroic kitsch and 'real' World of Darkness sensibilities. It's just grounded enough to be believable, and just absurd enough to be a metric ton of fun.<br /> <br /> Plus, lots of people love 80s cheese.<br /> <br /> Or in even shorter terms, they're just a lot of fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-02-2014, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T14:03:13-07:00","id":123987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/122598-mortal-remains-is-here?p=123832#post123832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know where you get that idea, they're more like Dog the Bounty Hunter.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can PUNCH OFF DEMONS' COVERS!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T14:28:54-07:00","id":124000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Tin Soldier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/122598-mortal-remains-is-here?p=123829#post123829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, could someone please explain to me just who the Knights of St. Adrian are? Because all I've got so far is that they're ridiculous 80s action heroes. Which sounds a little too... ridiculous for this level of love. Don't get me wrong, I love ridiculous, but it tends not to mesh all that well with standard WoD fluff. So what's so great about them?</div> </div> </div> </div> Demons are clever, subversive manipulators. They're a subtle problem, inclined to working within layers upon layers of lies and cover. The Knights of Saint Adrian are a blunt solution, a sort of divine shock troop that the Unchained will not expect and cannot cope with. They ignore all of the secrecy. They smash the problems to bits. It's chaos in a way that most Demons likely don't expect and can't respond to well. It's a wonderful mirror to Demon: the Descent; what could more opposite from a spy than a fucking roadie with magic fists?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T14:29:47-07:00","id":124001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/122598-mortal-remains-is-here?p=123987#post123987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They can PUNCH OFF DEMONS' COVERS!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, that will never not be satisfying to hear. It's just pure absurdity spun in gold.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/122598-mortal-remains-is-here?p=124000#post124000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Demons are clever, subversive manipulators. They're a subtle problem, inclined to working within layers upon layers of lies and cover. The Knights of Saint Adrian are a blunt solution, a sort of divine shock troop that the Unchained will not expect and cannot cope with. They ignore all of the secrecy. They smash the problems to bits. It's chaos in a way that most Demons likely don't expect and can't respond to well. It's a wonderful mirror to Demon: the Descent; what could more opposite from a spy than a fucking roadie with magic fists?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is so much more succinct than what I said. Can I hire you to speak for me from now on?<br /> <br /> Coincidentally, do you sound anything like Jeremy Irons?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-02-2014, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T14:43:51-07:00","id":124008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/122598-mortal-remains-is-here?p=124000#post124000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Demons are clever, subversive manipulators. They're a subtle problem, inclined to working within layers upon layers of lies and cover. The Knights of Saint Adrian are a blunt solution, a sort of divine shock troop that the Unchained will not expect and cannot cope with. They ignore all of the secrecy. They smash the problems to bits. It's chaos in a way that most Demons likely don't expect and can't respond to well. It's a wonderful mirror to Demon: the Descent; what could more opposite from a spy than a fucking roadie with magic fists?</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing that's worth pointing out though - the Knights often do their own investigation work and have no Endowment to help with that. Even when they don't the G-M or something else had to do so.<br /> <br /> So the Knights aren't really &quot;chaos in a way Demons don't expect&quot;. They're more like &quot;you screwed up, the G-M found you, here's the consequences&quot;. Something that is very much within the Unchained's world-view.<br /> <br /> They're still doomed either way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T14:53:46-07:00","id":124018,"title":"","content":"It is chaos of an unexpected sort. The job may come from the angels, and as such a certain amount of information is handed to them, but demons tend to be active busybodies even with staying quiet, so it's still work to find them on the field.<br /> <br /> On top of that, even the God-Machine and its' angels operate with similar subtlety to demons-that's where it's a spy game. THe Knights-no, I'm calling them the other name-The Sidearms* contrast even Angels in just how blunt they are. Destroyers before and after aren't this blatant.<br /> <br /> So it's a bit of both.<br /> <br /> *I keep wanting to call them Dogs or Wolves, but that's my first Sidearm's fault(Rudolph Schwan, aka Fenrir, hunting down the demon Wednesday).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-02-2014, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T16:12:59-07:00","id":124092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/122598-mortal-remains-is-here?p=123987#post123987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They can PUNCH OFF DEMONS' COVERS!</div> </div> </div> </div>So the hunters of the St. Adrian conspiracy are The Expendables?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T16:13:58-07:00","id":124093,"title":"","content":"Demons are on a whole other level. They have a pretty decent power scale. Humans generally aren't much of a threat unless they're Stigmatic, and even then they don't get the heart racing like a pack of rabid cryptids or an angel. The Knights are kind of an empowerment fantasy; its powers the Unchained aren't used to coming from a direction they'd never expect. It's a human empowerment fantasy, really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T16:30:25-07:00","id":124108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/122598-mortal-remains-is-here?p=124093#post124093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons are on a whole other level. They have a pretty decent power scale. Humans generally aren't much of a threat unless they're Stigmatic, and even then they don't get the heart racing like a pack of rabid cryptids or an angel. The Knights are kind of an empowerment fantasy; its powers the Unchained aren't used to coming from a direction they'd never expect. It's a human empowerment fantasy, really.</div> </div> </div> </div>With delicious irony fueling it if you say the God-Machine is behind it. The reason it's a human empowerment trip is because you're backed by a thing that's really out to disempower humanity on the whole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/122598-mortal-remains-is-here?p=124092#post124092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So the hunters of the St. Adrian conspiracy are The Expendables?</div> </div> </div> </div>...Pretty much, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T18:54:32-07:00","id":124205,"title":"","content":"Hey, I h